<% layout("/layouts/boilerplate") %>

<div class="row my-5">
    <div class="col-12 col-lg-8 mx-auto">
        <div class="p-4 p-md-5 rounded-4 shadow-sm" style="background: var(--wl-surface); border: 1px solid var(--wl-border);">
            <span class="wl-badge wl-badge--verified mb-2">Legal & Terms</span>
            <h1 class="wl-display wl-h2 mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
            <p class="wl-muted small">Effective: September 2026 &bull; Version 2.0</p>
            <hr class="my-4" style="border-color: var(--wl-border);">

            <h3 class="wl-h3 mb-2">1. Acceptance of Terms</h3>
            <p class="wl-muted" style="line-height: 1.8;">
                By accessing or using Wanderlust, you agree to comply with and be bound by these Terms of Service and our Privacy Policy.
            </p>

            <h3 class="wl-h3 mt-4 mb-2">2. Host & Guest Responsibilities</h3>
            <p class="wl-muted" style="line-height: 1.8;">
                Hosts are responsible for ensuring their property descriptions, pricing, and availability are accurate. Guests agree to treat reserved properties with respect and abide by all posted house rules and local regulations.
            </p>

            <h3 class="wl-h3 mt-4 mb-2">3. Bookings & Cancellations</h3>
            <p class="wl-muted" style="line-height: 1.8;">
                When a booking is confirmed, a binding agreement is formed between guest and host. Cancellations are subject to the stay's cancellation policy.
            </p>

            <h3 class="wl-h3 mt-4 mb-2">4. Limitation of Liability</h3>
            <p class="wl-muted" style="line-height: 1.8;">
                Wanderlust serves as an intermediary platform connecting hosts and guests. Wanderlust is not liable for property damage, personal injury, or unforeseen circumstances beyond our reasonable control.
            </p>

            <div class="mt-5">
                <a href="/listings" class="wl-btn wl-btn--primary">Back to Stays</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
